On Sat, Apr 19, 2014 at 2:28 PM, Gleki Arxokuna
<gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>wrote:

>
>
> The point is that camxes was indeed a major change in the language but it
> hadnt much to do with CLL that's why few mention it when speaking about
> changes in lojban.
>
>
"not much to do with CLL" is something of an exaggeration... It only
deviates from CLL in relatively marginal or doubtful cases.



> however, i wonder why {relmast} is no longer valid. How can it even break
> self-segregation?
>

It's because of the final double consonant -st, not because it breaks
self-segregation. The current version of the morphology will accept almost
anything for cmevla, so probably the test was done with an older more
strict version.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

